# Future Directions — Local-to-Global Structure of Fibonacci Apparition Ranks

## Synthesis

This cycle read the Fibonacci **rank of apparition** (entry point) `z(p) = fibEntry p` through a
sheaf-theoretic, local-to-global lens, and turned the catalog's entry-point machinery into a small
but coherent "structure sheaf of Fibonacci divisibility". The organizing observation is that for
each modulus `p` the global divisibility section `U(p) = {n | p ∣ F n}` is *exactly* the principal
ideal generated by the single local datum `z(p)` (`fib_divisibility_principal`). Because a
principal ideal is recovered from its generator, every join/meet identity among the sets `U(p)`
descends verbatim to the arithmetic function `z`. Local-to-global is here literal: a global section
is reconstructed from one stalk-level number.

On that footing we proved (file `Catalog/Pythagorean/FibEntryLocalGlobal.lean`, `sorry = 0`):

- **Stalk = principal ideal** (`fib_divisibility_principal`): `{n | p ∣ F n} = {n | z(p) ∣ n}`.
- **Global gluing from prime-power charts** (`fibEntry_eq_lcm_primePow`): for every `n > 0`,
  `z(n) = lcm_{p ∣ n} z(p^{v_p(n)})`. This strictly generalizes the catalog's
  `FibCarmichaelStructure.fibEntry_squarefree` from squarefree `n` to *all* `n`: the global entry
  point is the join (lcm) of its values on the prime-power charts of `n`.
- **Local sections glue** (`fib_prod_dvd_iff_forall`): for a pairwise-coprime family of moduli,
  the product divides `F n` iff each factor does — the compatibility/gluing axiom of the
  divisibility presheaf.
- **Overlap cocycle** (`fibEntry_coprime_obstruction`): for coprime `m, n`,
  `z(m)·z(n) = z(m·n)·gcd(z(m), z(n))`. The deviation of `z` from strict multiplicativity is
  precisely the gcd "overlap" term — the obstruction to gluing local entry points into a strict
  product, vanishing exactly when the local apparition sets are disjoint.

These build directly on `Catalog/Novelty/FibonacciEntryPointDuality.lean`
(`fib_dvd_iff_fibEntry_dvd`) and `Catalog/Novelty/FibCarmichaelStructure.lean`
(`fibEntry_coprime_mul`, `fibEntry_prod_coprime`, `fibEntry_squarefree`).

